= Schema — Simple =

A '''schema''' is a set of rules describing how data should be structured.

For example, a Person record might require:

<pre>
name: text
birth date: date
email: text
</pre>

A schema can say:
* which fields exist;
* what type of value each field uses;
* which fields are required;
* how records are connected.

A schema is not the same as the data itself.

It is also not always the same as an [[Ontology/Simple|ontology]].

A schema usually focuses on structure and validation.

An ontology usually focuses more on meaning and relationships in a domain.

